  "description": "For the next generation of shredders. Whether on the trails or the ride to school, the Speed 20 is solid little mountain bike that is ready to tackle the trails and cover some distance. With disc brakes and front suspension, it's a great ride to gain confidence on and off the pavement. The frame is light but with durable construction, striking a balance of fun and function. And it's designed to stand up to the learning curve of trail riding, so it's destined for heirloom status.\n\nMEC designed frame uses 6061 aluminum for a durable yet light construction\n\nSR Suntour XCT suspension fork has 63mm of travel and preload adjustment for improved tracking\n\n8-speed gearing gives a great range for trails or hills\n\nShimano Altus shifter and derailleur give reliable gear changes\n\nTektro Jr. hydraulic disc brakes have lots of stopping power in all weather\n\nWTB Ranger tires bite into dirt and gravel, and roll smoothly on paved surfaces\n\nReflective details help keep your little rider seen\n\nBikes are covered by MEC's Rocksolid Guarantee and Bike Service Agreement. You can bring your bike to any MEC bike shop for free adjustments and minor maintenance for a year after purchase\n\nMEC bikes were designed in Canada. Everything from the frames to the graphics was developed at the MEC Head Office in Vancouver, BC\n\nDue to challenges with supply chain, components may be substituted for comparable parts at any time. The listed build is how MEC intended your bike to arrive, though the manufacturer may need to make a tweak or two to get you riding sooner",
